<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa's Alliance ups yr earnings 38 pct.</title>
<headline>S.Africa's Alliance ups yr earnings 38 pct.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended February 28, 1997.</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, (cts)		    10.4	   vs   7.5</p>
<p>    Profit after tax	    7.09	   vs  4.49</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			 9.51	   vs  4.69</p>
<p>    Tax			     2.42	   vs  .202</p>
<p>    Interest paid		 1.73	   vs  1.56</p>
<p>    Turnover		     85.63	   vs 59.38</p>
<p>Full name: Alliance Pharmaceuticals Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company has decided to award capitalisation shares to ordinary and &quot;N&quot; ordinary shareholders. The terms of the award will be announced on or about Monday July 7, 1997. Shareholders will be allowed to decline the capitalisation award and instead may elect to receive a cash dividend of two cents per share for the year ending February 28, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
